<https://kerfors.github.io/early-clinical-design-research/remapcap-design-modules/imports/upstream_import> a owl:Ontology .

ns2:BFO_0000001 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "entity"@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000116 "BFO 2 Reference: In all areas of empirical inquiry we encounter general terms of two sorts. First are general terms which refer to universals or types:animaltuberculosissurgical procedurediseaseSecond, are general terms used to refer to groups of entities which instantiate a given universal but do not correspond to the extension of any subuniversal of that universal because there is nothing intrinsic to the entities in question by virtue of which they – and only they – are counted as belonging to the given group. Examples are: animal purchased by the Emperortuberculosis diagnosed on a Wednesdaysurgical procedure performed on a patient from Stockholmperson identified as candidate for clinical trial #2056-555person who is signatory of Form 656-PPVpainting by Leonardo da VinciSuch terms, which represent what are called ‘specializations’ in [81"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf owl:Thing .

ns2:BFO_0000002 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "continuant"@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000116 "BFO 2 Reference: Continuant entities are entities which can be sliced to yield parts only along the spatial dimension, yielding for example the parts of your table which we call its legs, its top, its nails. ‘My desk stretches from the window to the door. It has spatial parts, and can be sliced (in space) in two. With respect to time, however, a thing is a continuant.’ [60, p. 240"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns2:BFO_0000001 .

ns2:BFO_0000016 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "disposition"@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000116 "BFO 2 Reference: Dispositions exist along a strength continuum. Weaker forms of disposition are realized in only a fraction of triggering cases. These forms occur in a significant number of cases of a similar type."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns2:BFO_0000017 .

ns2:BFO_0000017 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "realizable entity"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns2:BFO_0000020 .

ns2:BFO_0000020 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "specifically dependent continuant"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns2:BFO_0000002 .

ns2:IAO_0000030 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "information content entity"@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000111 "information content entity"@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000115 "A generically dependent continuant that is about some thing."@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000116 "Pier: 'data, information or knowledge'. OR 'representation'"@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000412 ns2:ogms.owl ;
    rdfs:subClassOf owl:Thing .

ns2:IAO_0000104 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "plan specification"@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000115 "A directive information entity with action specifications and objective specifications as parts, and that may be concretized as a realizable entity that, if realized, is realized in a process in which the bearer tries to achieve the objectives by taking the actions specified."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns2:IAO_0000033 .

ns2:OBI_0001755 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "selection criterion"@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000111 "selection criterion"@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000112 "rats should be aged between 6 and 8 weeks and weight between 180-250grams"@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000114 ns2:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns2:IAO_0000115 "A directive information entity which defines and states a principle of standard by which selection process may take place."@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000117 "Person: Philippe Rocca-Serra"@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000118 "selection rule"@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000119 "OBI discussion summarized under the following tracker item : http://sourceforge.net/p/obi/obi-terms/678/"@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns2:IAO_0000033 .

ns2:OBI_0500000 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "study design"@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000111 "study design"@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000112 "a matched pairs study design describes criteria by which subjects are identified as pairs which then undergo the same protocols, and the data generated is analyzed by comparing the differences between the paired subjects, which constitute the results of the executed study design."@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000114 ns2:IAO_0000122 ;
    ns2:IAO_0000115 "A plan specification comprised of protocols (which may specify how and what kinds of data will be gathered) that are executed as part of an investigation and is realized during a study design execution."@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000116 "Editor note: there is at least an implicit restriction on the kind of data transformations that can be done based on the measured data available." ;
    ns2:IAO_0000117 "PERSON: Chris Stoeckert" ;
    ns2:IAO_0000118 "experimental design"@en ;
    ns2:IAO_0000232 "rediscussed at length (MC/JF/BP). 12/9/08). The definition was clarified to differentiate it from protocol."@en ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ns2:IAO_0000104 .

rdfs:comment a owl:AnnotationProperty .

